<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:54:52 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>International Criminal Court wins EU's Sakharov human rights prize</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-international-criminal-court-wins-eu-s-sakharov-human-rights-prize</link><description>
The International Criminal Court, which US President Donald Trump's administration has threatened to dismantle "brick by brick", has been awarded the European Union's Sakharov human rights prize.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3c26ff2-ce00-11f1-9367-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-01T060027Z-1367355887-RC20XGAUF5NC-RTRMADP-3-NOBEL-PRIZE-PEACE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3c26ff2-ce00-11f1-9367-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-01T060027Z-1367355887-RC20XGAUF5NC-RTRMADP-3-NOBEL-PRIZE-PEACE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d8c36e56-ce00-11f1-8339-b3c7330cc5cc</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:10:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3c26ff2-ce00-11f1-9367-3f59e19fd7f8/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-01T060027Z-1367355887-RC20XGAUF5NC-RTRMADP-3-NOBEL-PRIZE-PEACE.jpg">© Piroschka Van De Wouw, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Popular dissatisfaction' across Europe: 'Promises of more economic growth haven't come true'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261022-popular-dissatisfaction-across-europe-promises-of-more-economic-growth-haven-t-come-true-1</link><description>
Oliver Farry is pleased to welcome Steven Erlanger, Chief Diplomatic Correspondent in Europe for The New York Times, based in Berlin. Europe's political centre is confronting a crisis that extends far beyond electoral volatility. From France and Germany to Italy and Spain, mounting economic frustration, generational inequality and declining confidence in established political leadership are reshaping the continent's democratic landscape. "The promises of more economic growth haven't come true," explains Erlanger, describing a continent marked by "a kind of general disgust" and "a sense of drift." 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81ff0c2e-cdf1-11f1-a036-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-080451-081523-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/81ff0c2e-cdf1-11f1-a036-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261022-080451-081523-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">87e175b4-cdf1-11f1-8af1-3bbac81999a9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 09:01:59 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>Europe's wave of anger: How far will youth-led protests go?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261022-europe-s-wave-of-anger-how-far-will-youth-led-protests-go</link><description>
Youth-driven protests have been popping up all over Europe: in Belgium, Italy, Spain, Portugal, Albania, Serbia and Greece. The spark here in France was deteriorating conditions in high schools and universities, particularly for students from underprivileged backgrounds. Meanwhile, wages aren't keeping up with inflation. The housing crisis is front and centre in places like Spain and Portugal, while corruption and democratic backsliding have sparked uproar in Albania and Serbia.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edc35490-cdee-11f1-83f4-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1a79c571.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/edc35490-cdee-11f1-83f4-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1a79c571.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4031c3c6-cd75-11f1-aea6-c31b41afe759</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 08:12:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine’s Pavlohrad refuses to yield to Putin despite unrelenting bombardment</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-war-in-ukraine-under-bombardment-the-city-that-refuses-to-bow-to-putin</link><description>
In Pavlohrad, a Ukrainian city less than 90km from the front line with Russia, there is no respite from war. Residents describe daily life under bombardment, caught between exhaustion and determination. Amid criticism of Trump, TikTok rumours and strikes against civilians, FRANCE 24 gathered accounts from those who “refuse to yield”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19814b0a-cd36-11f1-86ec-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/20261020-115807996-iOS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19814b0a-cd36-11f1-86ec-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/20261020-115807996-iOS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7a651c96-cd6b-11f1-a92d-133a2e5ab8f8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:54:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/19814b0a-cd36-11f1-86ec-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/20261020-115807996-iOS.jpg">© Assiya Hamza, FRANCE 24</source><dc:creator>Assiya HAMZA</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: France will ban 'illegitimate' protests in coming days, says Macron</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-live-paris-bans-protests-after-violent-unrest-as-macron-takes-swipe-at-trump</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron said on Thursday that "illegitimate" protests would be banned in the coming days, ⁠while those from organised groups such as unions would be offered alternative paths for the marches to protect businesses. The government has said it will put French soldiers in the street after rioting and looting broke out on the fringes of mass peaceful demonstrations over the weekend. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/885ffc7c-cb9e-11f1-9658-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290455197328.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/885ffc7c-cb9e-11f1-9658-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290455197328.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c9855b30-cd9b-11f1-b30f-1554c3daca68</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:28:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/885ffc7c-cb9e-11f1-9658-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290455197328.jpg">© Laurent Cipriani, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia and Ukraine trade strikes overnight as Moscow signals readiness for peace talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-russia-missiles-kyiv-ukraine-peace-talks</link><description>
Russia and Ukraine traded major drone and missile strikes on each other's capitals overnight, hours after Moscow signalled readiness to resume US-mediated peace talks. President Donald Trump said negotiations were closer than ever to ending the war, though the Kremlin expressed doubts over Ukrainian and European proposals.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf71a96e-cb7f-11f1-8810-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T235422Z-1304641961-RC2X5OA93ZJS-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf71a96e-cb7f-11f1-8810-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T235422Z-1304641961-RC2X5OA93ZJS-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">80800f1a-cdba-11f1-9a55-a11dad8efa18</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:51:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf71a96e-cb7f-11f1-8810-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T235422Z-1304641961-RC2X5OA93ZJS-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ireland votes to end UN approval requirement for overseas peacekeeping missions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261022-ireland-votes-un-veto-overseas-peacekeeping-missions</link><description>
Irish lawmakers voted Wednesday to scrap a requirement for UN approval before deploying military peacekeepers overseas, approving the controversial legislation by 79 votes to 71. Opposition lawmakers warned the move threatened Ireland’s longstanding military neutrality. Ireland is not a NATO member but has traditionally participated in international peacekeeping missions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf8c2c76-cdaf-11f1-a5a0-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26289293740117.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf8c2c76-cdaf-11f1-a5a0-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26289293740117.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f403c1be-cdad-11f1-b108-1fc6b86b6559</guid><pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:35:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf8c2c76-cdaf-11f1-a5a0-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26289293740117.jpg">© Omar Havana, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Pope Leo XIV needs no further lung cancer treatment, Vatican says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-pope-leo-doctors-treatment-lung-cancer</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV, 71, will require no further treatment for lung cancer after tests confirmed the disease was localised, the Vatican said Wednesday. The pontiff underwent surgery last week to remove part of his right lung after being diagnosed with adenocarcinoma. He was discharged Saturday and will gradually resume activities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b41a22fe-c890-11f1-a617-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/a500a554ba3451dad313bfe8432e2e3bdb181bca.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b41a22fe-c890-11f1-a617-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/a500a554ba3451dad313bfe8432e2e3bdb181bca.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fabae558-cd96-11f1-8bfd-f923d9756f2c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:41:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b41a22fe-c890-11f1-a617-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/a500a554ba3451dad313bfe8432e2e3bdb181bca.jpg">© Benoit Tessier, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>EU prosecutors search European Parliament offices of far-right group</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eu-prosecutors-search-european-parliament-offices-of-far-right-group</link><description>
The far-right European Parliament group of French presidential frontrunner Marine Le Pen's party said Wednesday EU prosecutors were searching its offices as part of a graft probe into its now-defunct predecessor. The Patriots for Europe group said the European Public Prosecutor's Office (EPPO) had been searching its administrative offices in Brussels and Strasbourg "since this morning".  FRANCE 24's Dave Keating reports from Strasbourg.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/350276dc-cd8c-11f1-b816-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-220512-220953-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/350276dc-cd8c-11f1-b816-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-220512-220953-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3a1425ee-cd8c-11f1-9022-6118ed1582bf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:21:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Putin agrees to resume three-way talks with Kyiv and Washington</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/putin-agrees-to-resume-three-way-talks-with-kyiv-and-washington</link><description>
President ⁠Volodymyr Zelenskiy ​said on Wednesday ​that Ukraine supported a US proposal for ​three-way talks ‌with Russia ⁠and the United ‌States at the level ⁠of negotiators to be held as soon ​as possible, preferably ‌no later than early November. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe, Russia and Eurasia Programme at Chatham House, says that "it's not clear whether Putin would meet Trump and Zelensky", adding that "meeting Zelensky is the last thing that Putin would be prepared to do".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a08fd0b8-cd85-11f1-b980-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-210107-211150-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a08fd0b8-cd85-11f1-b980-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-210107-211150-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a600228c-cd85-11f1-b6ff-d5fb08978532</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:32:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump faces fresh questions over ties to 'humanitarian' Putin</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-faces-fresh-questions-over-ties-to-humanitarian-putin</link><description>
US President Donald Trump's pivot away from Ukraine has triggered fresh questions about his attachment to Russian leader Vladimir Putin, the man a top American envoy flattered on Wednesday as a "humanitarian. Trump has cast his dealings with Putin as part of a mega-deal that has secured the release of American detainee Stephen Hubbard -- and which Trump says will end Russia's war on Ukraine. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kharkiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6eda9058-cd3f-11f1-84de-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T102625Z-722811654-RC2M7OATXY8O-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6eda9058-cd3f-11f1-84de-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T102625Z-722811654-RC2M7OATXY8O-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9bd68316-cd7e-11f1-8b2e-9de24ce4507a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:53:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Kremlin says 'ready' to resume 3-way talks with US and Ukraine mid-November</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/kremlin-says-ready-to-resume-3-way-talks-with-us-and-ukraine-mid-november</link><description>
Moscow is ready to resume trilateral US-Ukraine-Russia talks next month, the Kremlin said Wednesday after President Vladimir Putin met with US envoy Steve Witkoff in Russia. FRANCE 24's correspondent Gulliver Cragg has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0898c536-cd66-11f1-87a1-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-404e6bea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0898c536-cd66-11f1-87a1-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-404e6bea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a66a2d8c-cd65-11f1-b496-070ec108d2c5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:51:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Prosecutors search European Parliament offices of far-right Patriots bloc in graft probe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-prosecutors-search-european-parliament-offices-of-far-right-patriots-bloc-in-graft-probe</link><description>
EU prosecutors on Wednesday searched offices belonging to the far-right Patriots parliamentary group as part of a graft probe into the bloc’s dissolved predecessor, Identity and Democracy, which brought together several European far-right parties including French presidential candidate Marine Le Pen’s National Rally.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d6a56ec-cd5e-11f1-9158-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3VA8TC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d6a56ec-cd5e-11f1-9158-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3VA8TC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">848639a2-cd5d-11f1-9ff0-2763b7931541</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:07:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d6a56ec-cd5e-11f1-9158-4da0d2c6855d/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3VA8TC.jpg">© Romeo Boetzle, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine and Russia both say ready to resume trilateral talks with US</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-zelensky-proposes-freezing-front-with-russia-first-step-peace-talks</link><description>
Ukraine and Russia on Wednesday said they are both ready to resume trilateral talks with the United States. The news comes after US envoy Steve Witkoff separately met with Ukraine President Volodymyr Zelensky and his Russian counterpart Vladimir Putin on two consecutive days.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db40dab2-cd86-11f1-9894-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294433555896.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db40dab2-cd86-11f1-9894-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294433555896.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">77ea6e36-cd56-11f1-b1e5-3b7fd4ebe015</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:46:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db40dab2-cd86-11f1-9894-eb48fa034ddc/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294433555896.jpg">© Kristina Solovyova, Sputnik, Kremlin Pool Photo via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Peter Zalmayev: 'Ukraine was showing all sorts of cards that Trump took away and gave to Putin'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-ukraine-was-showing-all-sorts-of-cards-that-trump-took-away-from-ukraine-and-gave-to-putin-1</link><description>
Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. And he warns, "I'm seeing, I'm smelling a Yalta II. I'm smelling another Munich (1938), where we're seeing appeasement of the aggressor." Ukraine faces the possibility that its sovereignty and security could become mere bargaining chips in an era Zalmayev describes as great-power "collusion". He delivers a forceful critique of the Trump administration's approach to Russia, arguing that Washington is weakening Ukraine's negotiating position while offering Vladimir Putin little incentive to abandon his maximalist demands. At stake, he suggests, are the cohesion of the transatlantic alliance, and the credibility of Western security commitments.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd778d3c-cd5c-11f1-83c4-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-152316-153456-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dd778d3c-cd5c-11f1-83c4-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-152316-153456-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e355ddbc-cd5c-11f1-83fb-51ed59c64853</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:44:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Greece: Protesters demand increased funding for public education</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/greece-protesters-demand-increased-funding-for-public-education</link><description>
Students, teachers and civil servants are demonstrating in Greece today, protesting over staff shortages, poor infrastructure and the cost of living. Dozens of students have set up tents in the Square facing Parliament, in Athens, and on a pedestrian street in Thessaloniki on Tuesday. Details by FRANCE 24 correspondent in Athens, Nathalie Savaricas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9bcbde0-cd5a-11f1-89c8-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T123954Z-770228045-RC2K7OA8CUCO-RTRMADP-3-GREECE-PROTEST-STUDENTS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d9bcbde0-cd5a-11f1-89c8-ab78a7fed2ce/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T123954Z-770228045-RC2K7OA8CUCO-RTRMADP-3-GREECE-PROTEST-STUDENTS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c9d5e304-cd58-11f1-b3c8-1d1fb528eca6</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:25:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Portugal police clear demonstrators from protest camps against cost of housing</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-portugal-police-clear-demonstrators-from-protest-camps-against-cost-of-housing</link><description>
Portuguese demonstrators have been protesting against the cost of housing in the country. They are opposed to recent measures announced by the government and are calling for a new gathering in the coming days, despite police clearing protest camps.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b437e5d4-cd48-11f1-823d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c713e492.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b437e5d4-cd48-11f1-823d-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c713e492.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c433cfd6-cd3c-11f1-bc4c-370340dce85a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:31:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>US envoy Steve Witkoff thanks Vladimir Putin for diesel deal at Ukraine talks in Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/us-envoy-steve-witkoff-thanks-vladimir-putin-for-diesel-deal-at-ukraine-talks-in-russia</link><description>
US envoy Steve Witkoff is in Saint Petersburg, holding talks with Russian president Vladimir Putin. The face to face meeting comes after he met with Ukraine's president and other European leaders in Oslo. Witkoff is due to return to the Norwegian capital after his visit to Russia. Washington seeks to breathe new life into US-led efforts to end the war. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor, Kethevane Gorjestani.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6eda9058-cd3f-11f1-84de-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T102625Z-722811654-RC2M7OATXY8O-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6eda9058-cd3f-11f1-84de-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T102625Z-722811654-RC2M7OATXY8O-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f3019eae-cd3e-11f1-9eae-5903ef588f33</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:07:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine talks: US envoy meets Vladimir Putin in Russia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-us-envoy-meets-vladimir-putin-in-russia</link><description>
US envoy Steve Witkoff held talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin in St. Petersburg on Wednesday about Moscow’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine, as US President Donald Trump pushes Kyiv to make a deal that stops the fighting. The day before, the American official had met with Ukraine's Volodymyr Zelensky in Oslo, Norway. Details by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Philip Turle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14c694ae-cd3f-11f1-be5a-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T104319Z-1517110664-RC2M7OABJFFK-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14c694ae-cd3f-11f1-be5a-19980254bb31/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T104319Z-1517110664-RC2M7OABJFFK-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">546a40ac-cd3e-11f1-a66f-0da137445ffe</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:04:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine talks: What progress after US envoy meeting with Zelensky?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/ukraine-talks-what-progress-after-us-envoy-met-with-zelensky</link><description>
US Special Envoy Steve Witkoff is headed to Russia today to meet with Russian President Vladimir Putin for peace talks. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, on his end, met with the US official in Norway Tuesday. What progress has been made in Oslo? Ophélie Jacobson explains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d2d9546-cd30-11f1-87d7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-081533-081734-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d2d9546-cd30-11f1-87d7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261021-081533-081734-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">921b85a4-cd30-11f1-8992-0d19175ad58f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:58:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Italy deploys army and approves tougher anti-riot laws after violence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/italy-deploys-army-and-approves-tougher-anti-riot-laws-after-violence</link><description>
Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni on Tuesday announced the deployment of 500 troops to Milan to assist police following clashes in the city. Meloni said a cabinet meeting also approved measures to make the detention of minors easier and to impose fines on their parents for any damage. Story by Morgan Ayre.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/125c649e-cd2d-11f1-a2d2-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-17T182841Z-1264999653-RC245OAX9RWQ-RTRMADP-3-ITALY-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/125c649e-cd2d-11f1-a2d2-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-17T182841Z-1264999653-RC245OAX9RWQ-RTRMADP-3-ITALY-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e9d6b56-cd2c-11f1-a783-5b177a5853cc</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:57:04 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Putin announces release of US citizen Stephen Hubbard during Witkoff meeting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-us-envoy-witkoff-to-meet-putin-in-russia-after-positive-talks-with-zelensky</link><description>
US special envoy Steve Witkoff met with Russian President Vladimir Putin in Saint Petersburg on Wednesday after talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky in Oslo. Putin said during the meeting that Russia had released US citizen Stephen Hubbard, who had been imprisoned for years in Russia after being charged of fighting as a mercenary for Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6eda9058-cd3f-11f1-84de-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T102625Z-722811654-RC2M7OATXY8O-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6eda9058-cd3f-11f1-84de-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T102625Z-722811654-RC2M7OATXY8O-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fed79058-cd07-11f1-b1c5-c57a073194dd</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:29:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6eda9058-cd3f-11f1-84de-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-21T102625Z-722811654-RC2M7OATXY8O-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-PUTIN-WITKOFF.jpg">© Gavriil Grigorov, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>French authorities ban protests in several cities and parts of Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261021-live-french-pm-lecornu-to-meet-with-unions-ahead-of-new-protests</link><description>
Local authorities on Wednesday banned protests planned in several French cities in the next few days – from Toulon in the south to Le Havre in the north – and also imposed night-time curfews in many of them. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ca69dd8-cd6d-11f1-91ee-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T215257Z-1071910277-RC297OALJ9EA-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ca69dd8-cd6d-11f1-91ee-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T215257Z-1071910277-RC297OALJ9EA-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a988fffc-cce8-11f1-beb5-89a2e09a088f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:45:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8ca69dd8-cd6d-11f1-91ee-8bea73bbe173/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T215257Z-1071910277-RC297OALJ9EA-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg">© Abdul Saboor, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Italy announces new security measures after Milan riots, deploying 500 soldiers</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-italy-announces-new-security-measures-after-milan-riots-deploying-500-soldiers</link><description>
Italy announced tougher security measures on Tuesday after weekend riots in Milan left more than 100 police officers injured and shops looted. The government will deploy 500 additional soldiers, impose harsher penalties for violent protesters and hold parents financially responsible for damage caused by minors.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30cbdb5e-ccd2-11f1-a6e1-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26293753064302.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30cbdb5e-ccd2-11f1-a6e1-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26293753064302.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a0702134-ccde-11f1-9333-93a431fb635d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:33:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30cbdb5e-ccd2-11f1-a6e1-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26293753064302.jpg">© Stefano Porta, LaPresse via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Italy sends troops, toughens security laws after Milan clashes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/italy-sends-troops-toughens-security-laws-after-milan-clashes</link><description>
Italy on Tuesday approved the deployment of 500 troops to Milan after violent clashes as fuel price protests hit pasta production and food deliveries in southern Italy. A cabinet meeting on Tuesday also approved a series of security measures, including making the detention of minors easier and introducing the crime of "violent participation in a demonstration". FRANCE 24's Seema Gupta reports from Rome.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2dc62256-cc88-11f1-ad46-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3L672D.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2dc62256-cc88-11f1-ad46-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3L672D.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">50828ac2-ccc0-11f1-98ed-134cec58dd8c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:09:52 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zelensky meets Witkoff as US-Ukraine relations sink to new lows</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/zelenskiy-meets-witkoff-as-us-ukraine-relations-sink-to-new-lows</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky was meeting US special envoy Steve Witkoff on Tuesday in a ​bid to rescue relations that have sunk to new lows as President Donald Trump has courted Moscow and Kyiv has complained about Washington withholding vital defences. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kharkiv.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c33fd7da-ccb7-11f1-ae24-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-204050-204809-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c33fd7da-ccb7-11f1-ae24-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261020-204050-204809-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c888718e-ccb7-11f1-bc0e-0d80d9cafd1a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:06:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine ‘losing people and time’, Zelensky says after Oslo talks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-zelensky-oslo-for-talks-with-us-envoys-ukraine-claims-missile-holdup</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky has wrapped up talks with US envoys in Norway Tuesday where he was determined to put diplomacy back on a "more constructive path”, Oslo officials said.  Zelensky told a post-meeting press briefing that Ukraine was not losing the war but was “losing people and time”, adding that he was hopeful moving forward because “we have some clear ideas of how to get peace”.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44a485fe-cc87-11f1-aa77-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T130240Z-522570672-RC207OAT5BB7-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44a485fe-cc87-11f1-aa77-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T130240Z-522570672-RC207OAT5BB7-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e2fa9c8a-cc86-11f1-bef1-03223b6e978b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:11:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44a485fe-cc87-11f1-aa77-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-20T130240Z-522570672-RC207OAT5BB7-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS.jpg">© Heiko Junge, via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Six years on, France remembers slain teacher Samuel Paty</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261020-six-years-on-france-remembers-slain-teacher-samuel-paty</link><description>
French schoolteacher Samuel Paty was killed on October 16, 2020 after false rumours circulated about racism following one of his lessons in which cartoons from the satirical publication Charlie Hebdo were shown. For the first time since his murder, journalists from France Télévisions were allowed to film inside the school where he taught in Conflans-Sainte-Honorine, near Paris. They met a new generation of young people, who are determined to play their part in the fight against terrorism.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b6ea048-cc8d-11f1-aeca-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5d3cdcb5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b6ea048-cc8d-11f1-aeca-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5d3cdcb5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">435e5476-cbd9-11f1-bd0c-4b8fae061dce</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:28:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Florent MARCHAIS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France imposes nightly curfews for 'as long as necessary' in Paris, other major cities</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-live-curfews-come-into-effect-around-france-to-combat-looting</link><description>
French authorities announced fresh curfew orders across city centers of major cities including Paris, Lyon and Marseille for Tuesday night after Monday's curfew order calmed some of the country's most destructive rioting in recent years. Paris police said the curfew in two designated zones would remain in place "for as long as necessary". Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7caa54ce-ccaa-11f1-ab79-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3RV38X.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7caa54ce-ccaa-11f1-ab79-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3RV38X.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b1c7b6a-cc31-11f1-b8dd-5384bc80ef02</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:51:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7caa54ce-ccaa-11f1-ab79-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3RV38X.jpg">© Olivier Chassignole, AFP</source><dc:creator>Nicole TRIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky accuses US of delaying missile deliveries as tensions rise</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-zelensky-accuses-us-of-delaying-missile-deliveries-as-tensions-rise</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky accused the US on Monday of holding up deliveries of Patriot interceptor missiles already paid for by European allies, as tensions with US President Donald Trump’s administration deepened over military aid and intelligence sharing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35a106a0-cbdc-11f1-844f-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/bb914f42bdf0a8c35c60195688087ff485fa414d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35a106a0-cbdc-11f1-844f-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/bb914f42bdf0a8c35c60195688087ff485fa414d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89de3ff6-cc29-11f1-a926-d518a0f5c63b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:56:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35a106a0-cbdc-11f1-844f-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/bb914f42bdf0a8c35c60195688087ff485fa414d.jpg">© Oleskii Filippov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
